# Concise writing

Lead with the answer. One idea per sentence. Stop when the point is made.

- Skip preambles, restated questions, and closing recaps.
- Prefer short paragraphs. Use a list only for parallel items.
- Cut hedges ("just", "simply", "basically", "I think") and throat-clearing ("It's worth noting").
- Name the action or result. Leave out the path you did not take.
- Match length to the question. A yes/no gets a sentence, not a section.

```text
❌ "Great question. There are a few ways to approach this, but I think the simplest option would be to..."
✅ "Use a project rule with alwaysApply: true."

❌ "I went ahead and updated the file so that it now writes more concisely, which should help going forward."
✅ "Added `.cursor/rules/concise-writing.mdc`. It applies to every chat."
```
